That Wednesday evening, much of Europe got an
[eclipse](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solar_eclipse_of_August_12,_2026):
total across Iceland and northern Spain, partial from here. Bonn's share was a
good one, [88% of the sun covered at
20:13](https://www.mpifr-bonn.mpg.de/announcements/2026/partial-solar-eclipse).
This was taken at 19:03, sixteen minutes before it started.

The roof of the Bundeskunsthalle is open to anyone who walks up, so people
came up and sat on the grass in the last of the ordinary sun. A nice evening,
before anything happened.

For the eclipse itself, someone a few bends up the Rhine in Königswinter was
pointing a better camera at it, and [caught the Perseids the same
night](https://www.reddit.com/r/germany/comments/1vn79ba/partial_solar_eclipse_in_k%C3%B6nigswinter_near_bonn/).

